'I started the way I would for a screen: a step-by-step flowchart. But voice conversations don’t follow a fixed order. Guests skip questions or ask things out of sequence, so the chart kept growing, and the team struggled to discuss it or agree on where to start.\n\nSo I changed my approach. With a data analyst, I used AI to analyze thousands of real calls and shared the insights with the team. Then I split ordering into one main flow and a set of edge cases.\n\nIn the next meeting, the team could finally see what was still unsolved, decide which cases the AI handles and which go to a human, and agree on a strategy for hotel requests.':'一開始，我用過去設計介面的方式，畫出一步接一步的流程圖。但語音對話不像介面有固定順序，客人會跳過問題、或不照順序提問，流程圖越畫越大，團隊也很難討論、收斂。\n\n於是我換了做法：和數據分析師一起用 AI 分析數千通真實通話，把觀察到的洞察分享給團隊，再把點餐流程拆成一條主流程和多個例外情境。\n\n在接下來的會議中，團隊終於能看清還沒解決的問題，決定哪些情境由 AI 處理、哪些轉給真人，並共同討論出回應飯店需求的策略。',

